/**
 * @mainpage Interstellar Documentation
 *
 * Welcome to the **Interstellar Engine** documentation.
 *
 * This documentation covers all major systems in the engine,
 * including input handling, graphics, configuration, data modeling,
 * and core gameplay interfaces.
 *
 * ## Getting Started
 * Explore the main systems and interfaces:
 * - @ref GameInterfaces "Game API"
 * - @ref InputSystem "Input System"
 * - @ref InterstellarData "Data Definitions"
 * - @ref InterstellarConfig "Configuration System"
 * - @ref InterstellarCore "Core Utilities"
 * - @ref PlatformImplementations "Platform Backends"
 * - @ref EngineInterfaces "Engine Extensions"
 *
 * Each system includes:
 * - Public interfaces and abstractions
 * - Internal engine extensions (used by the runtime)
 * - Platform-specific implementations (e.g., GLFW, SDL)
 *
 * ## Engine Architecture
 * The engine is composed of loosely coupled modules:
 * - **Core**: Logging, system initialization, diagnostics
 * - **Data**: Scientific models such as chemical elements or planetary parameters
 * - **Config**: JSON-serializable types for modding, tuning, or editor use
 * - **Input**: Abstract interfaces for keyboard, mouse, and device events
 * - **Rendering**: (WIP) Graphics subsystems for OpenGL/Vulkan (future work)
 *
 * ## Navigation Tips
 * - Use the **Modules** tab in the sidebar to browse logical groupings.
 * - Use the **Classes** tab to explore types and their responsibilities.
 * - Use the **Files** tab to trace where definitions are located.
 *
 * ## Contributing
 * All systems are designed with extensibility and testability in mind.
 * When adding new components:
 * - Follow the Doxygen group conventions (`@ingroup`)
 * - Document lifecycle and ownership clearly
 * - Favor composition over inheritance for config and data models
 */
